From 4488b77cf45fc132648388418e3e0c38a1f8038b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:53:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ptm: Play history power off entries, HOME Menu suspend/resume

The Activity Log counted 13 hours of Activity Log play time: the session of
2026-09-29 ended with "HOME Menu closed" and the next entry came the next day, so the
Activity Log treated the last application as running all night. A console never
logs the HOME Menu as closed at power off; it writes the special entry "3DS services
stopped" (title FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, event 1010), which the Activity Log takes as "all
titles closed".

Following the console's patterns (https://www.3dbrew.org/wiki/PTM_Savegame):
- Emulation stopping: applications still running are logged as closed, then
  "3DS services stopped". The HOME Menu is not logged as closed.
- A session that ended without that entry (crash, killed emulator) is ended at its
  last entry when emulation starts again.
- Starting an application while the HOME Menu runs logs "HOME Menu suspended" first;
  closing it logs "HOME Menu resumed".
- A title started again without exiting is logged as closed first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
